attribution: Anonymous traditional song of Spain and Mexico; the melody came from Spain in the colonial era and the song has circulated in the Americas for centuries, with no known author. Only the old first verse and refrain are used (not the 20th-century added verses), so melody and words are public domain. The B flat on "lucir" is a chromatic passing note and is expected to show as out-of-key.
